      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T22:28:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To me a safer change would be to allow only the first application to set whatever MTU it wants, and then subsequent requests would be rejected.\n\nAnd then, for LE Audio devices / devices with BT profiles, we as the stack would be the first application to request a large MTU. So for 3P peripherals used by only one app (which is the common case) we don\u0027t have to worry.",
      "parentUuid": "ce58647c_68d9a1cf",
      "revId": "e4dbc443c8d963e813ee04129b1242f7fa4e60cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
